**ScoreTrackr – Changelog**

---

**[v1.0] – 2025-08-15**
**Added**

* Created initial 2D array for storing student test scores
* Included sample dataset with students and 3 subjects (Math, Science, English)
* Set up basic project structure

---

**[v1.1] – 2025-08-29**
**Added**

* Defined rows as students and columns as subjects
* Added comments for clarity of data structure

**Changed**

* Improved formatting of dataset for better readability

---

**[v1.2] – 2025-09-12**
**Added**

* Implemented functionality to access a specific score using indexing
* Tested retrieval of values from the 2D array

---

**[v1.3] – 2025-10-03**
**Added**

* Implemented score update functionality

**Changed**

* Improved handling of data modification within the array

---

**[v1.4] – 2025-10-21**
**Added**

* Implemented average calculation for student scores
* Displayed computed averages

**Changed**

* Improved output formatting for readability

---

**[v1.4.1] – 2025-11-10 (Minor Patch)**
**Fixed**

* Minor issues in average calculation formatting
* Improved variable naming for clarity

---

**[v1.5] – 2025-11-26**
**Final (Python Version)**

* Final review of dataset logic and structure
* Cleaned up comments and formatting
* Prepared initial version for submission

---

**[v2.0] – 2026-02-16**
**Major Update (Web App Transition)**

**Added**

* Converted project into a web-based application (HTML, CSS, JavaScript)
* Created interactive user interface for inputting and displaying scores
* Added dynamic table rendering using DOM manipulation
* Implemented real-time score updates and retrieval

**Changed**

* Migrated from Python implementation to JavaScript 2D arrays
* Improved overall usability and accessibility of the system
* Refined project structure for web deployment (GitHub Pages)

---

**[v2.1] – 2026-03-01**
**Added**

* Introduced application branding: **ScoreTrackr**
* Added average column in the table for quick performance overview
* Improved UI design (layout, colors, button styling)

**Changed**

* Enhanced user experience with cleaner interface
* Improved input validation and feedback messages
